// clickbench.ron — hand-lowered physical plans for all 43 ClickBench queries.
// Lane: sqe-plans. Companion spec: ../PLANNER-SPEC.md (election laws, rewrite
// rules, fingerprint normalization, property system).
//
// SCHEMA (mirrors the sqe interface contract PlanNode; Rust types in
// ../tests/plans_parse.rs):
//   q            0-based ClickBench query id (= benchmarks/queries.sql line q+1)
//   family       primary stencil family from ENGINE-PLAN §3; `tags` carry
//                secondary family aspects where a winner spans two.
//   cols         attnos touched by the hot path (1-based line numbers of
//                src/hits_cols.tsv). Winner-hydration-only columns are NOT
//                listed (q23 hydrates all 105 for 10 rows — see notes).
//   pred         predicate tree; every leaf carries `fp` = the canonical
//                condcache fingerprint (PLANNER-SPEC §3.2) or None if the
//                leg is not fingerprintable. Fingerprint syntax:
//                "c<attno>:<op>:<canonical-const>".
//   group        group-key expressions (code-domain where the kernel stays
//                in codes; the planner must NOT lower these to bytes).
//   agg          aggregate specs over value expressions.
//   order        result ordering + limit/offset; tie: the study's canonical
//                tie-break (count DESC, key bytes ASC) unless KeyAsc.
//   params       named physical parameters. Fixed(..)/FixedStr(..) = query
//                text constants (safe to bake). Elect(law, inputs) = MUST be
//                stats-elected at run time — never bake a value (the
//                three-dead-metal-boxes rule). Laws are defined in
//                PLANNER-SPEC §1.
//   fingerprints summary list of the plan's fingerprintable legs (for the
//                condcache rewrite §2.4 and cross-query sharing).
//   kernel_oracle  the winning kernel this plan was cross-checked against:
//                variant, function, file, branch, best measured number.
//   notes        shape facts the family lanes parametrize against.
//   flags        menu misfits / hazards (also summarized in MISFITS below).
//
// MISFITS / FLAGS SUMMARY (queries whose winning kernel does not fit the §3
// menu cleanly — details in each entry's `flags`):
//   q5  — distinct computed on a 128-bit hash plane (probabilistic identity,
//         no byte verify); menu families assume exact identity.
//   q9  — one kernel spans two families (dense-group fused aggs + distinct
//         pipeline) with an atomic fetch_add merge the menu doesn't name.
//   q12 — hash-only equality (u128, no byte verify) + entry-grain predicate;
//         "two-level code agg" fits, but identity is probabilistic.
//   q16 — dual key currency (u64 empty-arm + u128 phrase-arm in one owner):
//         a semantic key-restriction rewrite the menu doesn't express.
//   q18 — depends on a persisted derived column (OrdRemap) with baked bit
//         widths 26/6/20 that are 10m-bank artifacts (assert-guarded);
//         bit widths MUST become elected values.
//   q29 — two stencils composed: algebraic rewrite THEN metadata answer;
//         neither menu row alone describes it.
//   q39 — CASE WHEN inside the group key: a derived-key element evaluated as
//         a code-domain select with ''-canonicalization to a reserved slot.
//   q21/q23 — condcache payload exceeds the GVerdict contract (q21 caches a
//         url-code sidecar; both bypass Skip/AllPass tags) — contract drift
//         to formalize in the engine's cache type.
//   q19 — answer lines are reconstructed from the predicate constant (valid
//         only for equality on the projected column itself).
//
(
    version: 1,
    attno_map: "src/hits_cols.tsv: line number = attno (1-based)",
    plans: [

